# ⚡ EASY - JavaScript DOM Mastery Series

A curated collection of **8 practical JavaScript exercises** designed to strengthen fundamental DOM manipulation skills, event handling, and logical thinking. Each project is self-contained in its own directory, making it easy to explore, run, and modify.

---

## 📚 Project Overview

| No | Project Name | Functionality | Core Concept |
|:--:|--------------|---------------|--------------|
| 1 | **EASY1-HELLO** | Displays "Hello World" text with an interactive link | `innerText`, `addEventListener`, link handling |
| 2 | **EASY2-NAMA** | Dynamically changes a name inside a paragraph | `.value`, DOM updates, `innerText` |
| 3 | **EASY3-CLICK** | Increments a displayed number on every button click | Event listeners, variable state (`let`) |
| 4 | **EASY4-Sembunyikan..?** | Toggles visibility of a hidden element (mystery feature) | `style.display`, conditional logic |
| 5 | **EASY5-COLOR** | Dynamically changes the color of text | `style.backgroundColor`, color manipulation |
| 6 | **EASY6-paragraf** | Modifies paragraph content using JavaScript | `innerHTML` / `innerText`, DOM replacement |
| 7 | **EASY7-TANGGAL** | Displays and formats the current date | JavaScript `Date` object, localization |
| 8 | **EASY8-bug...?** | Creative experimentation based on debugging concepts | Problem-solving, creative coding |

---

## 🧰 Technologies Used

- **HTML5** – Page structure
- **CSS3** – Basic styling (minimal)
- **JavaScript (Vanilla)** – All logic and DOM interactions

---

## 🎯 Objectives

This series was created to:

- Master fundamental **DOM manipulation** techniques.
- Practice using **event listeners** (`addEventListener`) for interactive UIs.
- Understand and utilize core DOM properties: `.value`, `.innerText`, `.style`, `.disabled`.
- Strengthen **conditional logic** (`if-else`) in real-world scenarios.
- Build confidence in writing clean, functional JavaScript without external libraries.

